\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Gait-validation sweep of the four production walking configurations against the 43-cycle locomotion reference library. The score is the production pipeline's cycle-shape kinematic score (0 denotes perfect agreement); the tuning-reference score is each configuration's evaluation on the tuning pipeline's walking reference, and the library mean averages the same score over all 43 references (among genuine gait cycles, higher scores indicate closer agreement).}}{171}{table.caption.61}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Pathway-removal sweep on the tuning-reference evaluation. The score is the production pipeline's cycle-shape kinematic score (0 denotes perfect agreement; $-25$ is the fixed no-cycle fallback, a failed evaluation that scores above every genuine gait in this table). The full-model rows repeat each configuration's unmodified production evaluation.}}{174}{table.caption.62}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Untuned spiking mirror versus its non-spiking twin at the same winner parameters, ground evaluation (16 s). The cycle knee minimum and stance fractions are computed over detected gait cycles; the kinematic score is the cycle-shape error metric of the production pipeline (0 denotes perfect agreement; higher scores indicate closer agreement). The spiking mirror carries mapped parameters only, with zero re-tuning.}}{180}{table.caption.64}%
